1
00:00:05,670 --> 00:00:09,740
(Hwang In Youp)

2
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:14,720
(Lee Hye Ri)

3
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:21,990
(Baek Sung Chul, Lee Yul Eum)

4
00:00:34,870 --> 00:00:38,870
(Dream To You)

5
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:40,170
(All people, events, and backgrounds are fictional.)

6
00:00:40,171 --> 00:00:41,179
(This drama includes footage created using AI.)

7
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:42,180
(Children and animals were filmed under strict safety guidelines.)

8
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:44,450
(Episode 7)

9
00:00:46,510 --> 00:00:50,220
(Jaejae Noodles)

10
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:54,220
- Going for a run? - Yes.

11
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:56,690
Why are you running this late at night?

12
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:58,760
So I don't run into him.

13
00:00:59,090 --> 00:01:00,389
You mean Su Bin?

14
00:01:00,390 --> 00:01:02,500
That's why you've been working from home lately?

15
00:01:03,130 --> 00:01:06,930
See? I told you I was right, didn't I? I was right.

16
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:09,100
A man's heart, right?

17
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:12,140
I told you it takes a man to know one.

18
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:14,940
You're right.

19
00:01:15,610 --> 00:01:18,010
You're asking for it. Darn you.

20
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:21,150
I got killed!

21
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:34,760
Sending the revised draft.

22
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:36,130
(Gyeongseong Love Song Screenplay Revised Draft)

23
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:37,770
Finally, a chance to see her.

24
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:44,970
I guess I still haven't gotten over her.

25
00:01:45,070 --> 00:01:46,070
Mister.

26
00:01:46,710 --> 00:01:50,040
- Focus. - Okay, okay. Here.

27
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:51,350
Okay.

28
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:56,620
Here, let me peel it for you.

29
00:01:58,690 --> 00:02:00,290
- Okay. - Thank you.

30
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:01,620
You're welcome.

31
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:05,360
- I got it out. - You did?

32
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:10,760
I really miss her.

33
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:12,600
Who?

34
00:02:14,130 --> 00:02:15,800
- A coworker. - A coworker?

35
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:19,310
- A friend. - I know.

36
00:02:19,870 --> 00:02:23,040
I only asked because it's weird to miss a coworker.

37
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:24,580
Why is it weird?

38
00:02:24,810 --> 00:02:28,480
They say that missing someone is the same as loving them.

39
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:32,250
And it's hard to love a coworker.

40
00:02:32,850 --> 00:02:34,620
You're really smart.

41
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:39,630
- Do you take after your mom? - Yes. I got my mom's brains,

42
00:02:39,730 --> 00:02:41,600
and they say I have my dad's looks.

43
00:02:42,830 --> 00:02:46,770
- I can see that. - Kim Sung Chan, Daddy's here.

44
00:02:46,830 --> 00:02:48,300
Dad.

45
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:50,969
- Dad. - Come here.

46
00:02:50,970 --> 00:02:52,140
There you go.

47
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:55,339
- Did you have fun with him? - Yes.

48
00:02:55,340 --> 00:02:56,979
Oh, my goodness.

49
00:02:56,980 --> 00:02:58,010
Sorry.

50
00:02:58,480 --> 00:03:00,510
A large group showed up at your mom's shop.

51
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:03,880
- It's okay. I was here for a bit. - I'll buy you a drink next time.

52
00:03:03,950 --> 00:03:06,020
- You don't need to. - Okay, say goodbye, "Seung Chan."

53
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:10,720
- Okay. Bye, "Seung Chan." - "Seung Chan"?

54
00:03:10,790 --> 00:03:14,290
Right. "Seung Chan." See you next time.

55
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:16,360
(Kim Sung Chan)

56
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:19,870
Let's go, let's go. Come on, this way. There we go.

57
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:21,700
- Go on. - Okay, we're going.

58
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:24,000
- Bye. - Bye.

59
00:03:24,270 --> 00:03:27,640
Oh my, you're so cute. Let's go, let's go.

60
00:03:30,010 --> 00:03:31,010
He's a good dad.

61
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:35,780
Grandma, Mom.

62
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:39,050
- I brought some twisted donuts. - I'm eating some right now.

63
00:03:39,350 --> 00:03:41,860
- What? - Yi Jae was just here.

64
00:03:42,460 --> 00:03:43,720
Why aren't you two hanging out these days?

65
00:03:45,890 --> 00:03:47,390
We're working separately.

66
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:51,700
So, what are you two doing?

67
00:03:52,330 --> 00:03:54,400
I'm studying for the driver's permit test,

68
00:03:54,470 --> 00:03:56,370
and she's learning to read and write.

69
00:03:57,570 --> 00:03:58,570
You're getting your license?

70
00:03:59,210 --> 00:04:01,740
I need to be able to go far away by myself now.

71
00:04:01,980 --> 00:04:03,140
You can go with me.

72
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:06,880
And I can teach you how to drive.

73
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:09,180
They say you should never learn how to drive from family.

74
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,290
Forget it. Look.

75
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:17,790
I still don't know it all, but I've definitely memorized this.

76
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:20,590
You wrote Mom and my names?

77
00:04:20,990 --> 00:04:22,430
You'll be writing poems soon.

78
00:04:24,730 --> 00:04:25,900
But...

79
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:28,369
Like this. And this.

80
00:04:28,370 --> 00:04:32,040
Hey, isn't that a 'bieup'? I know that one!

81
00:04:33,270 --> 00:04:34,910
It's 'Bin.'

82
00:04:35,210 --> 00:04:37,140
You haven't made a single mistake.

83
00:04:37,210 --> 00:04:39,410
Are you nervous because Su Bin is here?

84
00:04:40,510 --> 00:04:42,450
- Oh, honestly. - Bin.

85
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:44,420
Bin. There, right?

86
00:04:58,430 --> 00:04:59,430
Driver Kim.

87
00:04:59,830 --> 00:05:01,770
What are you doing waiting out here in the open like this?

88
00:05:01,940 --> 00:05:03,100
Your mother is here, isn't she?

89
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,810
Your father told me to bring her.

90
00:05:06,110 --> 00:05:08,280
If he wants to see her that badly, tell him to come himself.

91
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:10,280
Su Bin.

92
00:05:20,950 --> 00:05:23,390
If you come here again, I will call the police.

93
00:05:24,530 --> 00:05:26,690
Su Bin.

94
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:32,130
All right, the cast is all here. Now, let's get the video on screen.

95
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:34,330
Let's have the Catfish Man enter.

96
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:35,770
(The 7th Chain-Mate enters.)

97
00:05:40,910 --> 00:05:42,310
Hello.

98
00:05:43,010 --> 00:05:44,609
Hello.

99
00:05:44,610 --> 00:05:45,710
Hello.

100
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:48,920
I brought this.

101
00:05:51,990 --> 00:05:53,989
- Please, have a seat anywhere. - Have a seat.

102
00:05:53,990 --> 00:05:55,160
All right.

103
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:56,419
Yes. Where?

104
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:58,129
The wide shot is good.

105
00:05:58,130 --> 00:06:00,389
- Camera 3 and 4. - Sa Rang.

106
00:06:00,390 --> 00:06:01,559
- Please move to the left.. - this is absolutely huge.

107
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:04,300
The moment the Catfish Man walked in, the whole vibe changed.

108
00:06:04,330 --> 00:06:05,370
This is a massive hit.

109
00:06:05,930 --> 00:06:10,840
Yes, this is good. Let's get a group shot of the men...

110
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:13,170
and capture all their reactions.

111
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:15,740
They're reacting well to the Catfish Man.

112
00:06:16,510 --> 00:06:18,149
Yes, that's good.

113
00:06:18,150 --> 00:06:19,750
We're getting good audio pickup, right?

114
00:06:19,810 --> 00:06:20,810
I've looked forward to meeting you all.

115
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:22,350
Okay, production team, double-check...

116
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:24,020
the next interview and the outdoor set.

117
00:06:24,990 --> 00:06:26,890
Yes, that's good.

118
00:06:26,950 --> 00:06:29,960
We have some bread, grapes and egg tarts.

119
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:44,200
Sir.

120
00:06:45,070 --> 00:06:48,040
Yu Geon is only acting this way because he feels sorry.

121
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:51,950
And you're only doing it because you care about him.

122
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:56,820
And Yu Geon is so stubborn, you know.

123
00:06:57,120 --> 00:07:00,150
He could just ask my sister and Su Bin to cast him.

124
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:02,890
I wonder who he takes after to be so stubborn.

125
00:07:09,530 --> 00:07:10,530
He takes after me.

126
00:07:11,330 --> 00:07:12,330
I was the same way.

127
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:14,640
What good is all that pride?

128
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:18,440
I couldn't even ask anyone for a favour.

129
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:37,720
Sir.

130
00:07:38,230 --> 00:07:40,830
- Hello. - Su Bin. It's been a while.

131
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:42,600
Well...

132
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:44,970
Is Yi Jae with you?

133
00:07:45,430 --> 00:07:47,900
No. I'm by myself today.

134
00:07:48,540 --> 00:07:50,040
I see.

135
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:53,910
- Would you like to come in? - Oh, no. It's okay.

136
00:07:54,810 --> 00:07:57,180
Well, it's nothing much,

137
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:58,880
but I'd like Yi Jae...

138
00:08:00,050 --> 00:08:01,450
to take a look at this for me.

139
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:02,720
What is this?

140
00:08:02,780 --> 00:08:04,790
Don't feel pressured at all. All right?

141
00:08:05,620 --> 00:08:06,690
I'm leaving now.

142
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:10,260
- Wait, sir, this... - Go on inside.

143
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,770
(Yu Geon's Dream, Bus 31 - As Mail Carrier)

144
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:23,400
(Letter Of The Day - As Post Office Employee 3)

145
00:08:23,470 --> 00:08:24,470
(Low Voice - As Call Center Agent)

146
00:08:24,570 --> 00:08:25,770
(Late Arrival - As Flight Attendant)

147
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:26,840
(Going To School - As Student 3)

148
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:32,610
Sim Yu Geon. He's really worked hard.

149
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:35,720
(Sending the revised version.)

150
00:08:35,780 --> 00:08:37,450
He's seen it but hasn't replied.

151
00:08:40,090 --> 00:08:41,090
(Woo Su Bin)

152
00:08:42,820 --> 00:08:44,189
What's this?

153
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:45,190
Wait, no.

154
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:47,690
That makes it look like I've been waiting.

155
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:50,200
But I have been waiting, haven't I?

156
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:52,000
I was waiting for feedback.

157
00:08:56,970 --> 00:08:58,110
Hello.

158
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:00,910
What? Now?

159
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,709
To the studio?

160
00:09:02,710 --> 00:09:04,639
Oh my goodness, now?

161
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:07,780
Well... I need some time to get there.

162
00:09:07,850 --> 00:09:10,680
Okay. See you later.

163
00:09:12,890 --> 00:09:14,190
That was very natural.

164
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:18,390
See?

165
00:09:19,030 --> 00:09:21,290
So much for being colleagues.

166
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:33,470
Oh, I was wondering who that was.

167
00:09:34,370 --> 00:09:36,710
- You could've just come in. - It's called being polite.

168
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:38,080
Okay.

169
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:42,820
You're my...

170
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:45,320
Well...

171
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:48,320
- Can I come over here? - Sure.

172
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:54,760
Time for Plan B.

173
00:09:54,860 --> 00:10:01,870
(Ten Reasons Why A Contract Marriage Is Dangerous)

174
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:07,539
It has everything he starred, even the most recent shows.

175
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:08,880
Did Mr. Sim give this to you?

176
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:12,550
- It's a little over an hour long. - What? Has it been an hour already?

177
00:10:12,910 --> 00:10:14,410
Time flew by so fast.

178
00:10:14,710 --> 00:10:16,780
I know, right? The time I waited for you felt longer...

179
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:19,090
What?

180
00:10:19,690 --> 00:10:20,690
Well...

181
00:10:24,020 --> 00:10:26,060
It's probably because Yu Geon is such a good actor.

182
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,500
Yes, that's exactly what I was going to say.

183
00:10:32,330 --> 00:10:34,570
So, is there a role Yu Geon could play...

184
00:10:34,630 --> 00:10:35,700
A small role...

185
00:10:35,770 --> 00:10:37,640
Right, even a small role would be nice.

186
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:42,009
- No, I don't want that. - What?

187
00:10:42,010 --> 00:10:44,640
I hate when it feels like a handout.

188
00:10:45,050 --> 00:10:46,650
It wouldn't be fair to Yu Geon.

189
00:10:47,280 --> 00:10:48,380
Let's have him audition.

190
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:51,620
But he won't want to audition if I'm the one who asks.

191
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:52,820
If he gets the part, it'll be awkward,

192
00:10:52,890 --> 00:10:54,120
and if he doesn't, his feelings will get hurt.

193
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:56,790
Then it would be better to go through his agency.

194
00:10:57,060 --> 00:10:58,060
He doesn't have an agency.

195
00:10:58,490 --> 00:11:00,230
What? So he's been doing it all by himself?

196
00:11:00,530 --> 00:11:03,200
I mean, the difference between having an agency and not is huge.

197
00:11:03,330 --> 00:11:05,570
The audition opportunities themselves are completely different.

198
00:11:05,870 --> 00:11:09,270
Oh my goodness. I just don't understand him.

199
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:11,570
Seriously, actors with his looks and talent...

200
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:12,640
aren't a dime a dozen, you know.

201
00:11:13,370 --> 00:11:14,770
I just don't get it.

202
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:19,580
What?

203
00:11:19,581 --> 00:11:22,820
You know, you've always had a thing for his looks.

204
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:25,620
- To the point of making me jealous. - I was the one who was jealous.

205
00:11:26,550 --> 00:11:28,720
You said it yourself. That a face like Sim Yu Geon's...

206
00:11:28,790 --> 00:11:29,790
is made for the camera.

207
00:11:29,860 --> 00:11:32,730
When did I say that? I filmed your face way more.

208
00:11:32,990 --> 00:11:33,990
What?

209
00:11:33,991 --> 00:11:37,530
- Well... - That might be true.

210
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:38,770
We were dating...

211
00:11:40,930 --> 00:11:42,899
Well, that's all in the past.

212
00:11:42,900 --> 00:11:44,739
Besides, I can't resist pretty things...

213
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:45,740
What?

214
00:11:54,050 --> 00:11:55,380
Well, I should get going.

215
00:11:55,920 --> 00:11:58,120
- Where are you going? - Why? What?

216
00:11:58,220 --> 00:12:00,890
We need to have a meeting about the revised script.

217
00:12:01,390 --> 00:12:02,390
Right.

218
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:10,900
Should we do it here or there?

219
00:12:13,070 --> 00:12:14,070
Here?

220
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:24,840
(Name: Sim Yu Geon)

221
00:12:28,750 --> 00:12:30,380
Why would you agree to a contract like this?

222
00:12:32,090 --> 00:12:33,650
I don't see what I have to lose.

223
00:12:35,790 --> 00:12:37,990
You've already lost the most important thing.

224
00:12:38,660 --> 00:12:40,360
Because I'm the one who bought your heart.

225
00:12:41,190 --> 00:12:43,200
You must never fall in love with Ha Na.

226
00:12:43,730 --> 00:12:46,700
- But I don't have those feelings. - Of course you don't. I took them.

227
00:12:47,130 --> 00:12:48,340
And you'd better not have them in the future.

228
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:51,710
Isn't it amusing?

229
00:12:52,210 --> 00:12:56,280
That this little scrap of paper has your body and soul all tied up.

230
00:13:04,850 --> 00:13:05,850
Wow.

231
00:13:09,620 --> 00:13:12,360
Amazing. I love people like you.

232
00:13:12,430 --> 00:13:14,590
An investment in you shows immediate returns.

233
00:13:15,030 --> 00:13:16,499
It makes spending money satisfying.

234
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:17,530
Get in.

235
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:44,760
No. You're sitting next to me. Here.

236
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:46,760
Okay.

237
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:54,030
Is someone else joining us?

238
00:13:56,600 --> 00:13:58,540
- Hi. - Oh, you're here already.

239
00:14:03,580 --> 00:14:04,580
Sim Yu Geon.

240
00:14:06,750 --> 00:14:07,750
Su Bin.

241
00:14:09,550 --> 00:14:11,420
Do you two know each other?

242
00:14:12,590 --> 00:14:13,590
Perfect.

243
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:16,720
I'll be able to make it to the gym before it closes.

244
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:21,360
You must be happy to see him here.

245
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:23,630
- Right, Director Ian? - What do you think you're doing?

246
00:14:24,360 --> 00:14:25,370
What do you mean, what am I doing?

247
00:14:25,930 --> 00:14:27,830
I'm saying we should cast this young man as Mu Gyeom.

248
00:14:34,310 --> 00:14:35,310
What?

249
00:14:37,610 --> 00:14:39,310
You've really gotten more audacious over the years.

250
00:14:40,210 --> 00:14:42,280
First, you came up with an unscheduled audition,

251
00:14:43,050 --> 00:14:44,250
and now you're just casting roles yourself.

252
00:14:44,950 --> 00:14:45,950
The lead role, at that.

253
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:51,460
Director Ian, stop blocking the door and have a seat so we can talk.

254
00:14:52,390 --> 00:14:53,460
You sit down too.

255
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:58,000
Sim Yu Geon. Come out here.

256
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:06,070
Get out here now.

257
00:15:18,790 --> 00:15:20,120
I guess I won't make it to the gym.

258
00:15:28,060 --> 00:15:29,430
What are you doing here?

259
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:32,900
Yi Jae was so careful about even suggesting you audition.

260
00:15:33,830 --> 00:15:35,500
I guess we were worried for nothing.

261
00:15:36,470 --> 00:15:38,740
You should've just asked me or Yi Jae for help.

262
00:15:39,340 --> 00:15:40,940
It would have been much easier.

263
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:44,640
Rather than burdening the people I care about,

264
00:15:45,380 --> 00:15:48,680
- this is easier for me. - So you create a mess like this?

265
00:15:49,550 --> 00:15:51,550
I didn't expect to see you here.

266
00:15:53,090 --> 00:15:54,190
I'm sorry.

267
00:15:57,460 --> 00:15:59,090
If you were going to use your connections all along,

268
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:01,530
you should've done it when you were still young and naive.

269
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,760
After all the hardships you went through...

270
00:16:05,370 --> 00:16:06,370
Why now?

271
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:08,970
What do you know about it?

272
00:16:09,770 --> 00:16:12,540
You have no idea how I've managed to survive until now,

273
00:16:12,610 --> 00:16:13,870
so why do you say that?

274
00:16:14,310 --> 00:16:16,010
I should've done it when I was young and naive?

275
00:16:18,810 --> 00:16:21,210
Back then, I did the best I possibly could,

276
00:16:23,050 --> 00:16:24,520
and right now, this is the best I can do.

277
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:27,720
Fine.

278
00:16:29,160 --> 00:16:31,690
But take a good look in the mirror.

279
00:16:32,660 --> 00:16:34,860
Is that the face of someone who's doing their best?

280
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:38,770
Sim Yu Geon.

281
00:16:40,100 --> 00:16:41,900
I never particularly liked you,

282
00:16:42,670 --> 00:16:43,840
but I have to admit, there was something admirable about you.

283
00:16:45,210 --> 00:16:46,270
But...

284
00:16:46,710 --> 00:16:48,170
not anymore.

285
00:17:03,220 --> 00:17:04,220
Ian.

286
00:17:05,930 --> 00:17:06,930
Hey.

287
00:17:07,430 --> 00:17:08,430
Hey, you.

288
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:12,470
Are you just going to walk out?

289
00:17:13,270 --> 00:17:14,700
First, just calm down.

290
00:17:15,340 --> 00:17:17,700
- Just listen to me. - You crossed the line too.

291
00:17:18,770 --> 00:17:20,570
Just like the audition of Oh Ha Na, you should have at least...

292
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:22,110
had the decency to sneak around behind my back.

293
00:17:22,210 --> 00:17:24,580
I thought he was going to audition.

294
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:27,450
And that he's a friend of yours? So isn't this a good thing?

295
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:30,580
Exactly. That means you're the one who stole his opportunity.

296
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:33,690
If it weren't for this deal, he could've landed any part...

297
00:17:33,750 --> 00:17:36,920
You have to give one thing up to get another.

298
00:17:37,390 --> 00:17:38,790
You have to protect Joo Yi Jae.

299
00:17:41,230 --> 00:17:43,600
Why are you bringing up Joo Yi Jae now?

300
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:47,170
What we have to do in this situation is...

301
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:48,970
accept Sim Yu Geon,

302
00:17:49,670 --> 00:17:51,140
and protect Joo Yi Jae. That's it.

303
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:54,040
- Hey. - Snap out of it.

304
00:17:54,870 --> 00:17:56,509
No matter what great awards you've won...

305
00:17:56,510 --> 00:17:59,910
or how spectacular your debut was, this is only your second film.

306
00:18:00,450 --> 00:18:01,780
A romance that's hard to get funding for?

307
00:18:01,850 --> 00:18:03,050
On top of that, a period drama?

308
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:06,290
And you're co-directing with an unproven rookie. Hey!

309
00:18:06,950 --> 00:18:08,859
You're doing everything you want to do right now.

310
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:10,120
Can't you give up that one thing?

311
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:16,430
If it weren't for CEO Ahn,

312
00:18:17,630 --> 00:18:19,930
it wouldn't have been easy for us to get this far.

313
00:18:21,470 --> 00:18:23,400
Let's remember our place.

314
00:18:24,670 --> 00:18:25,670
You're right.

315
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:29,210
"We're not in a position to do something like this."

316
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:31,810
You should have told me from the start, sir.

317
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:34,210
You said you had to do this no matter what.

318
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:37,580
So what was I supposed to do? You said it was your dream.

319
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:44,190
When you were just 22,

320
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:46,790
you were wandering around without a home...

321
00:18:46,860 --> 00:18:49,000
and came to me with just that one script.

322
00:18:49,060 --> 00:18:50,900
I still remember that day vividly.

323
00:18:53,570 --> 00:18:55,539
Just like you're trying to keep your promise to Joo Yi Jae,

324
00:18:55,540 --> 00:18:56,540
I'm also...

325
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:58,940
just trying to keep my promise to you.

326
00:18:59,010 --> 00:19:01,610
But since I lack the ability, this was the best I could do.

327
00:19:08,180 --> 00:19:09,420
I'm sorry.

328
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:13,650
I'm sorry, Ian.

329
00:19:32,170 --> 00:19:34,570
Come on in, everyone. The food's getting cold.

330
00:19:42,450 --> 00:19:43,450
Director Woo.

331
00:19:44,380 --> 00:19:45,790
You heard from CEO Seo, right?

332
00:19:47,390 --> 00:19:48,590
Cast Sim Yu Geon.

333
00:19:49,320 --> 00:19:51,890
Or are you going to drop Joo Yi Jae?

334
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:57,660
You're going to push for Sim Yu Geon no matter what,

335
00:19:58,700 --> 00:20:00,830
and I'm going to protect Joo Yi Jae no matter what.

336
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:04,000
It seems like we already have our conclusion.

337
00:20:04,770 --> 00:20:05,840
I like that you're quick.

338
00:20:06,070 --> 00:20:08,040
I need to make things clear right here and now.

339
00:20:10,140 --> 00:20:11,140
Our movie...

340
00:20:12,610 --> 00:20:15,250
won't fall through just because we lose you,

341
00:20:15,310 --> 00:20:18,420
but it can't be made without Director Joo Yi Jae.

342
00:20:19,750 --> 00:20:21,889
You decided to invest after reading Director Joo's script,

343
00:20:21,890 --> 00:20:23,320
I'd appreciate it if you didn't tell us...

344
00:20:24,090 --> 00:20:25,530
to give up on her.

345
00:20:29,460 --> 00:20:32,269
I only gave it the time of day because it was your second project.

346
00:20:32,270 --> 00:20:33,400
Otherwise,

347
00:20:34,130 --> 00:20:36,170
do you think the script would have even made it to my desk?

348
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:41,740
Anyway, I got the answer I wanted, so I'll be going now.

349
00:20:42,780 --> 00:20:43,880
You're leaving already?

350
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:45,580
I have to go boxing.

351
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:48,110
Even if I leave now, I'll only get an hour in.

352
00:20:50,780 --> 00:20:52,250
What are you doing? Get up.

353
00:20:52,820 --> 00:20:53,890
Take care.

354
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:57,720
By the way.

355
00:20:58,620 --> 00:21:00,660
You're looking for a top star for the female lead, right?

356
00:21:01,290 --> 00:21:04,360
Since I saved you the time you would have spent looking for a male lead,

357
00:21:04,530 --> 00:21:08,800
spend that time on the female lead and make it a great film.

358
00:21:15,340 --> 00:21:18,440
- This rice wine... - I can't.

359
00:21:19,980 --> 00:21:21,250
You're really putting it away, aren't you?

360
00:21:21,380 --> 00:21:23,179
Who said they were having this earlier?

361
00:21:23,180 --> 00:21:24,820
- It was you. - No, it wasn't me.

362
00:21:25,650 --> 00:21:27,050
In Wook, coming back from work?

363
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:30,020
- Yes. - Aren't you dying to know his job?

364
00:21:30,090 --> 00:21:31,290
- I know, right? - Right.

365
00:21:31,360 --> 00:21:34,330
Hurry and get changed. We were just about to play Truth or Dare.

366
00:21:34,390 --> 00:21:37,760
I am a little tired. You all have fun.

367
00:21:40,030 --> 00:21:41,600
Right. It is understandable that he is tired.

368
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:44,540
- That's a shame. - I know.

369
00:21:44,600 --> 00:21:46,270
(Love Chain)

370
00:21:46,340 --> 00:21:49,240
The two of them are going out to the terrace. Follow them.

371
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:15,840
Is something wrong?

372
00:22:16,570 --> 00:22:17,940
You look troubled.

373
00:23:00,910 --> 00:23:03,520
Do not tell Yi Jae what we talked about earlier.

374
00:23:18,900 --> 00:23:20,200
Yu Geon, you are here.

375
00:23:21,330 --> 00:23:24,440
What is going on? Why do you look so handsome today?

376
00:23:25,270 --> 00:23:26,640
Did you play a handsome character?

377
00:23:28,410 --> 00:23:29,580
Why are you here?

378
00:23:31,110 --> 00:23:32,910
Well, you were not answering,

379
00:23:33,350 --> 00:23:34,949
and your motorcycle was parked out front of your home,

380
00:23:34,950 --> 00:23:36,550
so I thought you were home and came up.

381
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:40,390
But is something wrong?

382
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:43,190
You look a little down today.

383
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:45,789
I asked why you came.

384
00:23:45,790 --> 00:23:46,790
Right.

385
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:49,260
Give me your hand.

386
00:23:50,530 --> 00:23:52,000
Hurry up.

387
00:23:58,470 --> 00:23:59,470
(Oh Ha Na)

388
00:24:00,570 --> 00:24:03,510
Ta-da. I stole it from Mom's drawer.

389
00:24:04,410 --> 00:24:06,880
Now my real journey can finally begin.

390
00:24:07,250 --> 00:24:08,280
I did good, right?

391
00:24:13,590 --> 00:24:15,420
Showing up unannounced like this...

392
00:24:16,960 --> 00:24:18,490
is uncomfortable and unpleasant.

393
00:24:24,360 --> 00:24:26,900
Are you mad? Because I came without notice?

394
00:24:27,430 --> 00:24:28,600
I am sorry.

395
00:24:29,040 --> 00:24:31,300
- From now on... - And we should stop being friends.

396
00:24:34,210 --> 00:24:36,210
How can we be friends?

397
00:24:38,110 --> 00:24:40,450
Friendship is for people who are alike.

398
00:24:43,320 --> 00:24:44,580
Then...

399
00:24:46,850 --> 00:24:50,060
until now, what were we?

400
00:24:53,030 --> 00:24:54,190
Oh Ha Na and...

401
00:24:54,730 --> 00:24:55,760
Extra One.

402
00:24:59,730 --> 00:25:00,730
Leave.

403
00:25:23,420 --> 00:25:27,830
(Expiration Date: 10,000 Years)

404
00:26:04,260 --> 00:26:07,800
Oh my gosh, my stick figure storyboard turned into this quality?

405
00:26:08,100 --> 00:26:11,540
- Who is the storyboard artist? - Director Ian did it.

406
00:26:11,700 --> 00:26:12,870
Su Bin... I mean...

407
00:26:13,340 --> 00:26:15,780
Director Woo creates storyboards himself?

408
00:26:15,840 --> 00:26:18,280
Yes, he does not have a storyboard artist.

409
00:26:18,340 --> 00:26:20,050
He usually does them himself.

410
00:26:21,350 --> 00:26:24,650
No wonder. It is as if he took it straight from my mind.

411
00:26:29,560 --> 00:26:32,790
- You are here. - Jennie, can you give us a moment?

412
00:26:32,890 --> 00:26:34,060
Yes.

413
00:26:42,740 --> 00:26:45,540
- Why? - We're discussing it today,

414
00:26:46,140 --> 00:26:48,140
but I thought it would be best if you knew beforehand.

415
00:26:48,470 --> 00:26:49,680
What is it?

416
00:26:50,440 --> 00:26:51,810
The role of Mu Gyeom.

417
00:26:53,180 --> 00:26:55,510
Sim Yu Geon got it. It is confirmed.

418
00:26:55,780 --> 00:26:58,150
Yu Geon? The Sim Yu Geon that I know?

419
00:26:58,250 --> 00:26:59,550
Wait, how?

420
00:26:59,820 --> 00:27:02,220
I thought he was supposed to audition. Has he done it already?

421
00:27:03,320 --> 00:27:05,190
I heard Yu Geon is with Top Line Entertainment.

422
00:27:07,530 --> 00:27:08,730
As you know,

423
00:27:08,830 --> 00:27:11,930
CEO Ahn Soo Hee is our company's business partner.

424
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:14,400
Sim Yu Geon is with that agency?

425
00:27:14,570 --> 00:27:16,000
He seems to be a hot prospect.

426
00:27:16,200 --> 00:27:19,809
Especially since a powerful agency is backing him.

427
00:27:19,810 --> 00:27:23,640
What is with Sim Yu Geon? I feel so pleasantly betrayed.

428
00:27:25,480 --> 00:27:26,910
You seem really happy about it.

429
00:27:27,010 --> 00:27:31,320
Of course I am happy. But really, this is amazing.

430
00:27:31,380 --> 00:27:33,420
I guess if it is meant to be, it will be.

431
00:27:34,590 --> 00:27:35,820
If you are happy,

432
00:27:36,360 --> 00:27:37,360
then that is all that matters.

433
00:27:38,590 --> 00:27:39,590
I am sorry.

434
00:27:40,230 --> 00:27:42,660
I was only thinking about myself. Are you okay?

435
00:27:42,760 --> 00:27:45,160
We were going to have Yu Geon audition anyway.

436
00:27:45,970 --> 00:27:47,030
I am happy about it too.

437
00:27:55,170 --> 00:27:56,380
Hello.

438
00:27:56,880 --> 00:27:57,880
Oh, hello.

439
00:27:58,610 --> 00:28:00,980
- Keep up the good work. - Good work today.

440
00:28:08,690 --> 00:28:10,320
- Good work. - You too.

441
00:28:11,060 --> 00:28:12,060
Good work.

442
00:28:14,590 --> 00:28:16,660
Hey, Sim Yu Geon.

443
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:28,540
Hey, why the long face? We should be celebrating.

444
00:28:30,240 --> 00:28:32,440
- I'm sorry. - Sorry for what?

445
00:28:32,850 --> 00:28:34,780
I'm grateful that you're going to be Mu Gyeom.

446
00:28:34,850 --> 00:28:37,350
I know how much this movie means to you,

447
00:28:38,520 --> 00:28:40,020
and I know I shouldn't be like this.

448
00:28:41,490 --> 00:28:42,490
Yu Geon.

449
00:28:43,160 --> 00:28:46,559
That's just how life is sometimes. Sometimes, a meteorite...

450
00:28:46,560 --> 00:28:48,530
just crashes down right in front of you.

451
00:28:48,630 --> 00:28:51,460
It's not your land, so you wonder if it's really yours, right?

452
00:28:51,700 --> 00:28:53,470
But if you pick it up, it's yours.

453
00:28:53,870 --> 00:28:56,840
You seized this opportunity. So don't be timid.

454
00:28:56,940 --> 00:28:58,270
Our Mu Gyeom isn't like that.

455
00:29:02,040 --> 00:29:04,480
- Yi Jae, but... - I'm not trying to comfort you.

456
00:29:05,110 --> 00:29:06,179
I'm saying this...

457
00:29:06,180 --> 00:29:07,710
because you might think CEO Ahn helped you get cast.

458
00:29:08,450 --> 00:29:10,150
Do you think Woo Su Bin and I are pushovers?

459
00:29:10,280 --> 00:29:13,020
Do we seem like people who'd say yes to something we hate?

460
00:29:13,690 --> 00:29:15,020
It's not that, but...

461
00:29:20,930 --> 00:29:22,559
Hey, what is really wrong with you?

462
00:29:22,560 --> 00:29:24,200
Do you need a little smack to come to your senses?

463
00:29:28,730 --> 00:29:29,740
Yi Jae.

464
00:29:31,570 --> 00:29:33,310
There's no way I can hide this...

465
00:29:33,870 --> 00:29:35,870
and still be in your movie. It just doesn't feel right.

466
00:29:39,250 --> 00:29:40,610
The door is opening.

467
00:29:51,320 --> 00:29:53,290
Su Bin told me not to say anything.

468
00:29:56,460 --> 00:29:59,060
Actually, CEO Ahn made a demand.

469
00:30:00,200 --> 00:30:01,830
If they didn't cast me the lead,

470
00:30:04,300 --> 00:30:06,140
she said she'd have you removed as the director.

471
00:30:07,010 --> 00:30:10,110
Su Bin cast me to protect you.

472
00:30:18,950 --> 00:30:20,150
Hey, Director Woo.

473
00:30:21,820 --> 00:30:22,990
I thought you went home.

474
00:30:23,060 --> 00:30:25,120
I brought some kimbap for a late-night snack.

475
00:30:25,190 --> 00:30:27,490
I was getting hungry. Thanks.

476
00:30:37,170 --> 00:30:38,170
So did you...

477
00:30:38,770 --> 00:30:42,070
- go see Yu Geon? - Yes.

478
00:30:42,680 --> 00:30:47,310
He was so down in the dumps, so I gave him a good talking-to.

479
00:30:48,050 --> 00:30:49,320
He's talented.

480
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:52,080
- He'll do fine. - Yes.

481
00:30:52,790 --> 00:30:53,950
Thanks for the food.

482
00:30:54,890 --> 00:30:56,060
Thank you.

483
00:30:57,060 --> 00:30:58,320
This looks delicious.

484
00:31:00,430 --> 00:31:03,300
(Yu Geon's Dream)

485
00:31:08,430 --> 00:31:09,999
(Bus 31 - As Mail Carrier)

486
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:11,370
(Letter Of The Day - As Post Office Employee 3)

487
00:31:13,240 --> 00:31:15,640
I heard your father gave this to Su Bin.

488
00:31:16,510 --> 00:31:18,209
To ask him to take care of you.

489
00:31:18,210 --> 00:31:20,180
If you were going to use your connections all along,

490
00:31:20,780 --> 00:31:23,320
you should've done it when you were still young and naive.

491
00:31:23,750 --> 00:31:25,819
After all the hardships you went through...

492
00:31:25,820 --> 00:31:26,820
Why now?

493
00:31:26,821 --> 00:31:29,120
You've already lost the most important thing.

494
00:31:29,190 --> 00:31:31,390
Because I'm the one who bought your heart.

495
00:31:31,720 --> 00:31:33,830
You must never fall in love with Ha Na.

496
00:31:33,890 --> 00:31:36,700
Ta-da. I stole it from Mom's drawer.

497
00:31:37,630 --> 00:31:40,429
Now my real journey can finally begin.

498
00:31:40,430 --> 00:31:41,470
I did good, right?

499
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:51,840
(Expiration Date: 10,000 Years)

500
00:32:05,420 --> 00:32:07,930
(Simsim Seafood)

501
00:32:09,030 --> 00:32:10,430
(Actor Sim Yu Geon)

502
00:32:15,670 --> 00:32:17,900
Yes? Is something wrong?

503
00:32:19,370 --> 00:32:20,370
Dad.

504
00:32:21,640 --> 00:32:23,740
I'm speaking. What's wrong?

505
00:32:26,110 --> 00:32:28,750
I got cast.

506
00:32:29,380 --> 00:32:31,750
I'm the lead in a movie.

507
00:32:38,290 --> 00:32:39,290
Really?

508
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:43,400
Then why do you sound like that?

509
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:48,500
Because I'm happy.

510
00:32:52,300 --> 00:32:53,310
Is that so?

511
00:32:54,210 --> 00:32:55,469
All right. You've worked hard.

512
00:32:55,470 --> 00:32:56,510
Bye.

513
00:32:57,640 --> 00:32:58,640
Dad.

514
00:33:02,610 --> 00:33:03,980
Thank you.

515
00:33:33,180 --> 00:33:36,920
Are you really sure it's okay to stay at my house?

516
00:33:37,520 --> 00:33:40,020
If you ask me one more time, that'll be the tenth time.

517
00:33:40,450 --> 00:33:42,890
Stop asking. I'm telling you, I'm really fine.

518
00:33:43,060 --> 00:33:46,960
It's just, you're such an important person and this place is so shabby.

519
00:33:47,690 --> 00:33:51,130
When I worked abroad, I slept in worse places.

520
00:33:51,630 --> 00:33:54,270
I can even sleep outdoors as long as I have a sleeping bag.

521
00:33:59,470 --> 00:34:01,670
I'll put your luggage away.

522
00:34:15,720 --> 00:34:16,860
Where are you going?

523
00:34:18,090 --> 00:34:19,559
The New York shoot is next week.

524
00:34:19,560 --> 00:34:21,129
You know my schedule for next week,

525
00:34:21,130 --> 00:34:23,760
but I guess you didn't know my contract ended last week?

526
00:34:24,930 --> 00:34:27,400
Since when have we ever been sticklers for dates?

527
00:34:27,900 --> 00:34:29,230
I'm going independent.

528
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:32,770
- I'm not renewing my contract. - You're going to retire?

529
00:34:32,840 --> 00:34:35,670
No. Why would you think I'd quit this line of work?

530
00:34:35,740 --> 00:34:37,509
Because you've never wanted to do it.

531
00:34:37,510 --> 00:34:39,509
I probably never had a moment to think...

532
00:34:39,510 --> 00:34:41,010
about whether I wanted to or not.

533
00:34:42,650 --> 00:34:43,650
From now on,

534
00:34:43,651 --> 00:34:45,020
I'm going to live my life for myself.

535
00:34:45,620 --> 00:34:48,220
- Chae Yeon, is the luggage loaded? - Yes.

536
00:34:50,860 --> 00:34:52,820
Thank you for everything up to now, ma'am.

537
00:34:55,960 --> 00:34:57,500
Is it because of Sim Yu Geon?

538
00:34:59,870 --> 00:35:01,670
The way you're acting like a petulant teenager,

539
00:35:02,400 --> 00:35:03,640
isn't it because of him?

540
00:35:04,470 --> 00:35:06,770
Honestly, even if you have no one to turn to,

541
00:35:06,840 --> 00:35:08,910
how could you fall for a guy like that?

542
00:35:09,470 --> 00:35:11,810
- You'd be better getting therapy. - Mom.

543
00:35:11,880 --> 00:35:13,780
- What? - It's because of you, Mom.

544
00:35:13,950 --> 00:35:16,550
You make me feel like I'm suffocating.

545
00:35:17,120 --> 00:35:18,880
You were already digging into Sim Yu Geon's background?

546
00:35:18,950 --> 00:35:22,250
Good grief, listen to her. What do you take your mother for?

547
00:35:22,750 --> 00:35:23,819
You think I only looked into his past?

548
00:35:23,820 --> 00:35:26,490
I've also considered what he can do in the future.

549
00:35:27,030 --> 00:35:28,589
So don't mess with me.

550
00:35:28,590 --> 00:35:30,230
Just go clear your head for a day or two and come back.

551
00:35:30,730 --> 00:35:32,130
Gangneung should do the trick.

552
00:35:32,630 --> 00:35:36,030
Chae Yeon, use the company card. And don't just feed Ha Na sweets.

553
00:35:36,340 --> 00:35:37,340
Yes.

554
00:35:42,980 --> 00:35:44,379
Director Kang, release an article...

555
00:35:44,380 --> 00:35:45,640
that Ha Na is halting all activities.

556
00:35:46,450 --> 00:35:48,950
The reason? Just make something up.

557
00:35:57,160 --> 00:35:59,589
Ha Na, do you really have to go this far?

558
00:35:59,590 --> 00:36:01,389
Look. It's Jaden.

559
00:36:01,390 --> 00:36:03,099
Who's that? Should I go up to him?

560
00:36:03,100 --> 00:36:04,630
No, pass on him.

561
00:36:04,800 --> 00:36:06,600
I heard he's a CEO now.

562
00:36:06,730 --> 00:36:09,499
You can't trust people who are CEOs. Like my mom.

563
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:10,999
Okay, pass on the CEO.

564
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:13,569
Look. It's Director Ian.

565
00:36:13,570 --> 00:36:15,039
Should I get him? Should I go now?

566
00:36:15,040 --> 00:36:16,239
No.

567
00:36:16,240 --> 00:36:18,510
We can't approach him.

568
00:36:18,580 --> 00:36:21,349
But he's the director of Gyeongseong Love Song.

569
00:36:21,350 --> 00:36:23,150
Who else are you going to ask for the script?

570
00:36:25,820 --> 00:36:27,590
- Her. - What?

571
00:36:27,890 --> 00:36:29,590
Ha Na, wait!

572
00:36:39,730 --> 00:36:41,130
Director Joo Yi Jae.

573
00:36:44,740 --> 00:36:45,740
Oh Ha Na?

574
00:36:48,440 --> 00:36:50,340
But how do you know me?

575
00:36:50,510 --> 00:36:53,410
I was a huge fan of "Yi Jae Will Be There."

576
00:36:53,710 --> 00:36:56,450
And we also met at the department store event, right?

577
00:36:57,550 --> 00:37:00,520
Wouldn't you call this fate?

578
00:37:01,550 --> 00:37:03,520
- Fate? - Yes.

579
00:37:04,690 --> 00:37:06,930
So, what was it you wanted to talk to me about?

580
00:37:08,630 --> 00:37:11,000
Please give me the script for Gyeongseong Love Song.

581
00:37:11,060 --> 00:37:14,600
I thought CEO Ahn has it.

582
00:37:15,100 --> 00:37:18,140
Exactly. I should have stolen it.

583
00:37:18,470 --> 00:37:19,470
Excuse me?

584
00:37:20,670 --> 00:37:24,980
I really want to do that project, Director.

585
00:37:25,040 --> 00:37:27,510
I'm desperate. I've never felt this way before.

586
00:37:27,810 --> 00:37:29,580
- Really? - Yes.

587
00:37:31,520 --> 00:37:32,520
Can you hear it?

588
00:37:32,720 --> 00:37:34,990
Nan Yeong breathing and living inside of me.

589
00:37:36,020 --> 00:37:39,220
Yes, I can. I'll give it to you. How should I get it to you?

590
00:37:39,290 --> 00:37:41,960
- Should I give it to your manager? - No.

591
00:37:43,860 --> 00:37:45,560
Could I get your number, sis?

592
00:37:46,130 --> 00:37:47,200
"Sis"?

593
00:37:47,800 --> 00:37:51,100
It's flattering. Did Oh Ha Na just ask for my number?

594
00:37:52,270 --> 00:37:55,070
But in return, what happened today...

595
00:37:55,410 --> 00:37:57,010
is our little secret.

596
00:37:57,310 --> 00:37:59,510
- Okay. - Shhh.

597
00:38:01,310 --> 00:38:03,350
(Ahn Yoo Jung)

598
00:38:03,420 --> 00:38:04,650
(Im Min Joo)

599
00:38:04,720 --> 00:38:06,519
Of course, top actors are booked solid...

600
00:38:06,520 --> 00:38:08,490
for their next few projects.

601
00:38:08,550 --> 00:38:10,719
So at least there's a chance with actress Yoon Min Joo...

602
00:38:10,720 --> 00:38:14,590
- if we adjust the filming dates. - What about Oh Ha Na?

603
00:38:16,030 --> 00:38:17,259
Well...

604
00:38:17,260 --> 00:38:20,600
She's in talks for another project right now.

605
00:38:20,670 --> 00:38:21,969
No, there was an article a few days ago...

606
00:38:21,970 --> 00:38:23,400
saying she's taking a hiatus.

607
00:38:23,970 --> 00:38:24,970
Really?

608
00:38:27,610 --> 00:38:29,740
- Did I miss it? - I'm here.

609
00:38:30,380 --> 00:38:31,380
(Action.)

610
00:38:31,380 --> 00:38:32,380
Action.

611
00:38:36,980 --> 00:38:40,090
- What's going on? - You can't just come in here.

612
00:38:40,290 --> 00:38:41,850
- Is that a gun? - Excuse me.

613
00:38:45,190 --> 00:38:47,930
- Come on, we're in a meeting... - Comrades.

614
00:38:47,990 --> 00:38:50,630
- Nan Yeong? - Did she come dressed like that?

615
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:53,770
This is no time to be standing around.

616
00:38:54,000 --> 00:38:56,640
If we just sit around discussing the current state of affairs,

617
00:38:57,040 --> 00:38:58,540
nothing will change.

618
00:38:59,670 --> 00:39:03,840
Do you know how I felt when I blew up Wolhwajeong and left?

619
00:39:05,140 --> 00:39:09,310
I have no place to return to now. I can only move forward.

620
00:39:10,320 --> 00:39:11,820
Sadness is fleeting,

621
00:39:13,950 --> 00:39:15,990
but joy is eternal.

622
00:39:28,200 --> 00:39:29,530
That's right, comrade Nan Yeong.

623
00:39:29,770 --> 00:39:32,470
Let's march toward independence together.

624
00:39:41,180 --> 00:39:43,319
Why did you only appear now?

625
00:39:43,320 --> 00:39:44,349
Just as you said,

626
00:39:44,350 --> 00:39:46,380
it was like Nan Yeong is alive and breathing.

627
00:39:52,920 --> 00:39:54,230
Director Joo Yi Jae?

628
00:39:55,430 --> 00:39:56,430
Director.

629
00:40:04,670 --> 00:40:08,340
I've also prepared for Scene 34. Shall I perform it right now?

630
00:40:09,370 --> 00:40:12,610
Oh Ha Na, what do you think you're doing right now?

631
00:40:12,940 --> 00:40:15,810
I am confident that I can do a great job as Nan Yeong.

632
00:40:16,150 --> 00:40:18,520
- Give me the part. I'm begging you. - Yes.

633
00:40:19,520 --> 00:40:20,820
You were good.

634
00:40:21,320 --> 00:40:23,660
It was the same Oh Ha Na acting I've always seen.

635
00:40:24,160 --> 00:40:25,920
What I'm saying is, it wasn't special.

636
00:40:28,260 --> 00:40:31,930
Then may I tell you the special reason...

637
00:40:32,200 --> 00:40:33,730
why you should cast me?

638
00:40:34,930 --> 00:40:36,300
I'm curious.

639
00:40:39,300 --> 00:40:40,440
I...

640
00:40:42,270 --> 00:40:45,110
know someone who has lived a life just like Nan Yeong's.

641
00:40:46,340 --> 00:40:48,880
A child who, since she was young, had no dream of her own...

642
00:40:49,710 --> 00:40:51,480
and only lived as she was told.

643
00:40:54,190 --> 00:40:57,490
Not even knowing that her world was a small prison.

644
00:40:59,120 --> 00:41:02,960
Then she met someone like Mu Gyeom and realised.

645
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:07,900
Okay, you shoot the next take.

646
00:41:11,170 --> 00:41:13,940
If I break out of my world,

647
00:41:14,410 --> 00:41:16,680
there might be a bigger world out there.

648
00:41:17,210 --> 00:41:18,610
I want to live...

649
00:41:19,240 --> 00:41:21,250
in the same world as that person.

650
00:41:23,620 --> 00:41:28,020
So she blew up her entire world and ran out.

651
00:41:29,350 --> 00:41:30,460
I'm...

652
00:41:31,390 --> 00:41:34,530
no longer with Top Line Entertainment.

653
00:41:34,830 --> 00:41:36,490
I don't have an agency right now.

654
00:41:37,360 --> 00:41:39,760
And I plan to keep taking on challenges by myself from now on.

655
00:41:40,070 --> 00:41:43,970
I also requested this script from Director Joo Yi Jae myself.

656
00:41:44,800 --> 00:41:49,270
Wait, then does CEO Ahn Soo Hee know about this situation?

657
00:41:49,340 --> 00:41:50,580
She has no idea.

658
00:41:54,850 --> 00:41:56,150
So if...

659
00:41:57,320 --> 00:41:58,950
I become Nan Yeong,

660
00:41:59,220 --> 00:42:01,290
I think I'll have to hide it as much as possible...

661
00:42:01,420 --> 00:42:03,020
until filming starts.

662
00:42:03,820 --> 00:42:04,820
I'm sorry.

663
00:42:05,120 --> 00:42:06,520
Please help me.

664
00:42:07,260 --> 00:42:09,429
Help me live as Oh Ha Na,

665
00:42:09,430 --> 00:42:11,100
and no longer as Ahn Soo Hee's daughter.

666
00:42:14,800 --> 00:42:18,199
If the first step of my independence is to become Nan Yeong,

667
00:42:18,200 --> 00:42:20,510
I think it will give me great strength.

668
00:42:22,710 --> 00:42:24,180
Nan Yeong's independence,

669
00:42:25,140 --> 00:42:26,980
after all, has a happy ending.

670
00:42:31,680 --> 00:42:35,190
Could you please wait outside for a moment?

671
00:42:46,800 --> 00:42:48,870
Sorry for the wait. Have a seat.

672
00:43:00,350 --> 00:43:01,350
Oh Ha Na.

673
00:43:05,850 --> 00:43:07,090
Let's work together.

674
00:43:07,650 --> 00:43:09,290
I hope you can bring Nan Yeong's character to life.

675
00:43:12,190 --> 00:43:13,730
Thank you.

676
00:43:14,890 --> 00:43:16,160
I promise I will...

677
00:43:16,590 --> 00:43:19,060
do my absolute best to become the best Nan Yeong I can be.

678
00:43:19,630 --> 00:43:20,830
Do you know...

679
00:43:22,770 --> 00:43:24,870
why I didn't cast you back then?

680
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:29,070
You rejected me because my English wasn't good enough.

681
00:43:30,140 --> 00:43:33,480
The deciding factor was your attitude.

682
00:43:34,780 --> 00:43:38,250
You were like an elementary schooler,

683
00:43:39,120 --> 00:43:40,690
dragged here by your mom against your will.

684
00:43:43,350 --> 00:43:45,760
There's no fooling a director's eye, is there?

685
00:43:45,920 --> 00:43:47,890
But what I saw today was different.

686
00:43:49,130 --> 00:43:52,430
You were impressive, and now I have high hopes.

687
00:43:55,170 --> 00:43:56,470
Thank you.

688
00:43:58,700 --> 00:44:01,310
Anyway, as for the schedule going forward,

689
00:44:01,370 --> 00:44:03,710
it will be sent directly to you.

690
00:44:04,180 --> 00:44:05,680
Confidentiality is key.

691
00:44:06,140 --> 00:44:08,380
And don't mention it to your co-star, either.

692
00:44:08,550 --> 00:44:10,010
Oh, right. Mu Gyeom.

693
00:44:10,920 --> 00:44:12,350
Is it an actor I know?

694
00:44:13,120 --> 00:44:14,120
Who is it?

695
00:44:26,800 --> 00:44:28,770
- I told you not to come... - Why?

696
00:44:29,670 --> 00:44:30,970
Why did you do that?

697
00:44:31,300 --> 00:44:33,070
Why did you sign a contract with my mom?

698
00:44:36,570 --> 00:44:38,140
Because I have to become somebody.

699
00:44:40,010 --> 00:44:41,210
So, please.

700
00:44:42,210 --> 00:44:43,980
Just please, stay away from me.

701
00:44:46,520 --> 00:44:47,620
That contract...

702
00:44:50,050 --> 00:44:52,190
I signed it on the condition...

703
00:44:54,030 --> 00:44:55,490
that I would never fall in love with you.

704
00:44:58,960 --> 00:44:59,960
You're lying.

705
00:45:03,130 --> 00:45:04,500
No, I mean...

706
00:45:05,140 --> 00:45:06,640
What kind of contract is that?

707
00:45:08,010 --> 00:45:09,170
Yu Geon...

708
00:45:10,540 --> 00:45:11,780
Did you ever love me?

709
00:45:15,650 --> 00:45:16,650
No.

710
00:45:18,520 --> 00:45:19,520
Then why?

711
00:45:22,590 --> 00:45:24,360
What was there between us, then?

712
00:45:27,260 --> 00:45:28,260
I wonder.

713
00:45:30,860 --> 00:45:32,300
What was there between us?

714
00:45:36,400 --> 00:45:37,940
For me, there was definitely nothing.

715
00:45:54,590 --> 00:45:55,590
You're right.

716
00:45:56,720 --> 00:45:58,720
Birds of a feather flock together.

717
00:46:05,960 --> 00:46:07,670
I was wrong about you.

718
00:46:47,740 --> 00:46:48,810
(Mu Gyeom, Practice, Studying Japanese, Pronunciation)

719
00:46:49,340 --> 00:46:50,910
(Not too drunk, Not a drunkard, Just a slight stagger)

720
00:46:50,980 --> 00:46:52,340
(Deliver lines with a slight smile.)

721
00:46:52,410 --> 00:46:53,880
(When looking at Nan Yeong, pause a beat before reacting.)

722
00:46:53,950 --> 00:46:55,850
(Move smoothly. No shaky hands.)

723
00:47:04,290 --> 00:47:05,290
Yes, Dad.

724
00:47:10,130 --> 00:47:11,130
I'm here.

725
00:47:11,660 --> 00:47:12,660
You're here.

726
00:47:13,730 --> 00:47:16,100
Why are you here alone? Where's Joo Yeong Jae?

727
00:47:16,370 --> 00:47:17,840
I sent him to the market on an errand.

728
00:47:25,410 --> 00:47:26,410
Here.

729
00:47:28,180 --> 00:47:30,080
- What is it? - Go make this delivery first.

730
00:47:30,680 --> 00:47:32,020
I put the address on it.

731
00:47:34,650 --> 00:47:36,120
"3784..."

732
00:47:41,960 --> 00:47:42,990
Delivery.

733
00:47:47,870 --> 00:47:49,200
- Su Bin! - Yes.

734
00:47:50,000 --> 00:47:51,000
Come in.

735
00:47:51,370 --> 00:47:52,470
Why are you here?

736
00:47:52,770 --> 00:47:54,170
I asked your father to send you.

737
00:47:55,610 --> 00:47:56,610
You did?

738
00:47:56,710 --> 00:47:58,440
(CEO Seo In Wook, Actor Oh Ha Na)

739
00:47:59,340 --> 00:48:01,480
- It's a pleasure to work with you. - Me too.

740
00:48:02,280 --> 00:48:03,280
You're here?

741
00:48:06,580 --> 00:48:07,590
You're here.

742
00:48:09,190 --> 00:48:10,590
Do you two know each other?

743
00:48:10,660 --> 00:48:12,319
We used to.

744
00:48:12,320 --> 00:48:13,320
In the past.

745
00:48:14,330 --> 00:48:18,600
- From "Contract Marriage"? - I was the lead and he was Extra 1.

746
00:48:19,230 --> 00:48:20,230
Right?

747
00:48:21,400 --> 00:48:23,940
- What's going on? - We're here for a table read.

748
00:48:24,470 --> 00:48:27,870
Say hi. That's Nan Yeong, and this is Mu Gyeom.

749
00:48:28,940 --> 00:48:32,010
- What? - But has Mu Gyeom signed on yet?

750
00:48:33,280 --> 00:48:35,480
I wonder if my Mom signed it for him.

751
00:48:36,250 --> 00:48:38,650
Good question. Did he?

752
00:48:39,650 --> 00:48:41,890
That didn't sound like a question.

753
00:48:52,160 --> 00:48:55,469
"Scene 47. A street. Night. In the middle of all the commotion,"

754
00:48:55,470 --> 00:48:58,770
"Nan Yeong and Mu Gyeom in western attire walk side by side."

755
00:48:59,070 --> 00:49:01,740
"Despite the noise around them, the two walk slowly."

756
00:49:02,070 --> 00:49:04,810
"From every angle, you don't seem to have a care in the world."

757
00:49:04,880 --> 00:49:05,880
"What do you think?"

758
00:49:06,580 --> 00:49:08,350
"Not beneath the lanterns of Wolhwajeong,"

759
00:49:08,610 --> 00:49:10,149
"but I'm here, illuminated by this moonlight."

760
00:49:10,150 --> 00:49:11,250
"I look pretty charming, don't I?"

761
00:49:11,320 --> 00:49:13,720
"Why must you always turn everything into a joke?"

762
00:49:14,250 --> 00:49:17,090
Go, Gyeongseong Love Song.

763
00:49:25,930 --> 00:49:28,030
You two are so awkward.

764
00:49:28,730 --> 00:49:31,570
You're supposed to be in love soon. Why don't you try to get along?

765
00:49:32,070 --> 00:49:33,470
I'd love to.

766
00:49:35,070 --> 00:49:37,440
But I'm not sure if Yu Geon can.

767
00:49:37,840 --> 00:49:40,680
He may seem gruff, but he's a great guy on the inside.

768
00:49:41,650 --> 00:49:42,650
Is that so?

769
00:49:43,210 --> 00:49:45,580
I guess you're the type who's completely different on the inside.

770
00:49:47,950 --> 00:49:49,619
Your acting isn't bad,

771
00:49:49,620 --> 00:49:51,360
but you two don't seem to make any eye contact.

772
00:49:52,160 --> 00:49:53,520
Even if it's just a table read,

773
00:49:53,790 --> 00:49:56,060
you need to look at each other and match your pacing.

774
00:49:56,560 --> 00:49:57,659
If you're just going to read separately,

775
00:49:57,660 --> 00:49:58,830
you might as well have done it at home.

776
00:50:00,400 --> 00:50:02,530
- I'm sorry. - Sorry.

777
00:50:03,230 --> 00:50:05,300
But I actually found it amazing.

778
00:50:05,470 --> 00:50:06,939
How can you have such natural back-and-forth...

779
00:50:06,940 --> 00:50:08,010
without even looking at each other?

780
00:50:08,410 --> 00:50:09,640
Maybe they had a falling-out.

781
00:50:18,320 --> 00:50:19,320
Looks like I was right.

782
00:50:19,680 --> 00:50:21,789
They have to be friends first to fall out.

783
00:50:21,790 --> 00:50:22,920
I've seen them together.

784
00:50:23,690 --> 00:50:25,990
- They looked pretty close. - Really?

785
00:50:26,260 --> 00:50:27,660
If the friendship is over,

786
00:50:28,960 --> 00:50:30,230
maybe you should try falling in love.

787
00:50:30,760 --> 00:50:32,260
You're supposed to have a romance,

788
00:50:32,700 --> 00:50:34,170
but a broken friendship isn't right for that, is it?

789
00:50:34,800 --> 00:50:36,330
I'm sure they'll be different once the cameras roll.

790
00:50:36,970 --> 00:50:38,900
But falling in love will be even harder.

791
00:50:40,340 --> 00:50:41,470
Why don't you say something?

792
00:50:43,170 --> 00:50:44,610
Can you love me?

793
00:50:53,450 --> 00:50:56,050
I have to. The directors told me to.

794
00:50:57,090 --> 00:50:58,120
Aren't you, Ha Na?

795
00:50:59,890 --> 00:51:03,630
If it helps the show, I'm prepared to do anything.

796
00:51:05,300 --> 00:51:06,330
That's disappointing.

797
00:51:07,770 --> 00:51:09,170
Because I'm already in love.

798
00:51:18,140 --> 00:51:20,480
There's definitely something between them.

799
00:51:21,080 --> 00:51:23,850
- I'm dying to know, aren't you? - Not really.

800
00:51:23,920 --> 00:51:25,349
Hey, I'm telling you, I've never seen that look...

801
00:51:25,350 --> 00:51:26,350
on Sim Yu Geon's face before.

802
00:51:27,180 --> 00:51:31,060
It was like a cold, yet sad look in his eyes?

803
00:51:31,220 --> 00:51:32,820
Sounds more like a breakup than a falling-out.

804
00:51:33,560 --> 00:51:36,030
Perfect. That means they've already been in love.

805
00:51:36,360 --> 00:51:39,430
- Really? - We'll get great emotional depth.

806
00:51:40,300 --> 00:51:42,430
Should we shoot the breakup scene first?

807
00:51:44,100 --> 00:51:47,510
What you just said was really uncalled for.

808
00:51:48,770 --> 00:51:50,370
I'm saying, you don't need to worry about it so much.

809
00:51:51,310 --> 00:51:53,880
They can't hide their feelings on set either. It'll all come out.

810
00:51:54,080 --> 00:51:56,850
We just need to catch those moments and draw their emotions out.

811
00:51:57,110 --> 00:51:59,679
In that case, a love that's more like a war...

812
00:51:59,680 --> 00:52:00,990
would be even better.

813
00:52:01,790 --> 00:52:03,450
I also prefer that to a quiet romance.

814
00:52:03,550 --> 00:52:04,689
I write much better when my boyfriend and I...

815
00:52:04,690 --> 00:52:06,020
were at each other's throats.

816
00:52:06,120 --> 00:52:08,190
I wonder if it's because the emotional waves are bigger.

817
00:52:10,930 --> 00:52:12,660
- When? - What?

818
00:52:15,600 --> 00:52:18,740
Well, doesn't everyone date someone on campus in college?

819
00:52:18,800 --> 00:52:19,800
I haven't.

820
00:52:21,510 --> 00:52:22,510
Really?

821
00:52:23,510 --> 00:52:25,780
Hey, that's something you can only do at that age.

822
00:52:26,180 --> 00:52:27,350
What were you doing instead?

823
00:52:27,450 --> 00:52:29,880
I was busy carrying equipment on set...

824
00:52:29,980 --> 00:52:32,580
and bought one baguette to make it last the whole week.

825
00:52:32,680 --> 00:52:34,849
Okay, forget it. Let's move on.

826
00:52:34,850 --> 00:52:36,020
Was that really love, at that age?

827
00:52:40,220 --> 00:52:41,230
Then what about us back then?

828
00:52:45,800 --> 00:52:47,200
When we were 18 and 19.

829
00:52:48,830 --> 00:52:49,830
What was that then?

830
00:52:59,680 --> 00:53:00,810
It was love.

831
00:53:02,310 --> 00:53:04,720
Back when we were 18 and 19.

832
00:53:08,420 --> 00:53:09,550
And even now.

833
00:53:11,790 --> 00:53:12,990
I think it's love.

834
00:53:29,940 --> 00:53:31,240
I know...

835
00:53:32,210 --> 00:53:34,680
that you cast Yu Geon to protect me.

836
00:53:42,490 --> 00:53:44,120
- Yi Jae. - I'm not trying to blame you.

837
00:53:44,960 --> 00:53:46,120
I don't blame you anymore.

838
00:53:47,830 --> 00:53:48,890
It's just...

839
00:53:49,490 --> 00:53:51,430
what that feeling must be like...

840
00:53:52,730 --> 00:53:54,330
I've been thinking about it for a while.

841
00:53:56,570 --> 00:53:59,540
All great things start from something small, right?

842
00:54:00,340 --> 00:54:02,240
Just from you liking me,

843
00:54:03,040 --> 00:54:04,740
you came to love movies.

844
00:54:06,980 --> 00:54:07,980
But...

845
00:54:09,210 --> 00:54:10,550
the truly great thing...

846
00:54:12,020 --> 00:54:13,220
is that feeling, isn't it?

847
00:54:14,520 --> 00:54:15,850
And the feeling...

848
00:54:17,090 --> 00:54:18,320
you decided to hold back.

849
00:54:26,000 --> 00:54:27,700
Your feelings are so big...

850
00:54:28,570 --> 00:54:30,940
that I can't pretend I don't see them, Woo Su Bin.

851
00:54:33,970 --> 00:54:34,970
So...

852
00:54:37,510 --> 00:54:38,510
don't hold back.

853
00:55:23,250 --> 00:55:25,790
I'm already so nervous, what am I going to do?

854
00:55:26,920 --> 00:55:28,129
Even the masters...

855
00:55:28,130 --> 00:55:29,990
probably get nervous the day before their first shoot.

856
00:55:30,430 --> 00:55:33,100
- You think so? - So I come the day before...

857
00:55:33,160 --> 00:55:34,730
- Yes. - and in my head...

858
00:55:35,870 --> 00:55:38,870
- I run a simulation. - How?

859
00:55:39,300 --> 00:55:40,300
Here, look.

860
00:55:40,740 --> 00:55:43,840
The art department will be the first to arrive.

861
00:55:45,040 --> 00:55:47,140
- Okay. - They'll double-check the signs...

862
00:55:49,580 --> 00:55:53,080
and set up that steamy soup restaurant to look just right.

863
00:55:54,080 --> 00:55:55,490
- The cinematographer over there... - Yes?

864
00:55:55,590 --> 00:55:58,690
He'll be eating gummies, waiting for the setup to be done.

865
00:55:59,660 --> 00:56:01,860
Yes, Assistant Director. I'm on my way now.

866
00:56:03,730 --> 00:56:06,159
Always watch your step on set.

867
00:56:06,160 --> 00:56:07,730
Tripping over a cable is a huge deal.

868
00:56:07,800 --> 00:56:11,270
- Okay. - Watch out for lighting equipment.

869
00:57:16,830 --> 00:57:17,840
Yi Jae.

870
00:57:22,340 --> 00:57:23,370
And this here...

871
00:57:24,640 --> 00:57:26,840
is your seat, Director Joo Yi Jae.

872
00:57:27,140 --> 00:57:28,650
(Director Joo Yi Jae)

873
00:57:48,300 --> 00:57:50,300
(Director Joo Yi Jae)

874
00:57:54,070 --> 00:57:56,540
Sit here, and with everything you've got,

875
00:57:57,370 --> 00:57:58,380
call, "Ready."

876
00:57:58,880 --> 00:57:59,880
"Action."

877
00:58:01,480 --> 00:58:03,550
- Me? - Yes.

878
00:58:04,680 --> 00:58:07,420
(Director Woo Su Bin, Director Joo Yi Jae)

879
00:58:07,520 --> 00:58:08,750
Everyone...

880
00:58:09,650 --> 00:58:11,190
will be waiting for your cue.

881
00:58:15,260 --> 00:58:16,260
Go ahead.

882
00:58:28,170 --> 00:58:29,170
Ready.

883
00:58:38,420 --> 00:58:39,420
Action.

884
00:59:10,680 --> 00:59:12,720
(Dream To You)

885
00:59:12,850 --> 00:59:14,019
Directors, If you witness...

886
00:59:14,020 --> 00:59:15,519
any romantic behaviour between the staff members,

887
00:59:15,520 --> 00:59:16,520
please report it to me immediately.

888
00:59:16,590 --> 00:59:19,990
You need to stick right by my side and show my mom.

889
00:59:20,090 --> 00:59:21,729
Show her that there's absolutely no love between us.

890
00:59:21,730 --> 00:59:22,730
Relax.

891
00:59:22,860 --> 00:59:25,260
Oh Ha Na. Everyone, wrap it up.

892
00:59:25,460 --> 00:59:26,660
I'll drop out, CEO Ahn.

893
00:59:26,730 --> 00:59:29,670
This all happened because of your pathetic act of defiance.

894
00:59:29,730 --> 00:59:31,470
I'm sorry. This is my fault.

895
00:59:32,040 --> 00:59:34,199
I regret ever fixing you.

896
00:59:34,200 --> 00:59:35,810
I guess once something is broken,

897
00:59:35,910 --> 00:59:38,180
it's hard to be whole again.

898
00:59:38,780 --> 00:59:39,780
Yi Jae.